2026-08-22T02:04:04.4391063Z [36;1m# Infer each compiler default for the active R version from R CMD config,[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4391579Z [36;1m# then route it through ccache. Reading the resolved defaults preserves the[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4392110Z [36;1m# standard flags R selects per version (e.g. -std=gnu2x for C, -std=gnu++17[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4392601Z [36;1m# / -std=gnu++20 for C++); a plain "CC = ccache gcc" override would drop[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4393078Z [36;1m# them and silently downgrade the standard across the version matrix.[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4393563Z [36;1m# Inference uses an empty user Makevars so we always read the pristine[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4393989Z [36;1m# Makeconf defaults, never a value we just wrote.[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4394412Z [36;1m# Note: the versioned switches (CXX11..CXX23) intentionally come out as[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4394879Z [36;1m# bare "g++" with no -std flag. R keeps the standard in a separate[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4395613Z [36;1m# CXXnnSTD variable (CXX17STD = -std=gnu++17, ...) and applies it on top[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4396185Z [36;1m# at compile time, so wrapping only CXXnn with ccache is correct and we[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4396576Z [36;1m# must NOT pin -std here ourselves.[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4397028Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4397314Z [36;1m# On Unix, ccache is attached through a generated one-word wrapper[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4397908Z [36;1m# command (ccache-gcc, ccache-g++, ...) rather than the more obvious[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4398382Z [36;1m# "CC = ccache gcc" prefix. R-devel briefly could not cope with a[0m
