2026-08-22T02:04:04.4399807Z [36;1m# every package with compiled code, read R CMD config CC, kept only the[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4400269Z [36;1m# first word, and ran that. With "CC = ccache gcc" that left a bare[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4400727Z [36;1m# "ccache", and the check died with "ccache: invalid option -- 'E'".[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4401271Z [36;1m# https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/commit/ca19f35240517186ed447e773ee67b55e207cf27[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4401791Z [36;1m# https://bugs.r-project.org/show_bug.cgi?id=19130[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4402240Z [36;1m# Upstream has since dropped the truncation again, so the prefix works[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4402748Z [36;1m# once more -- but it takes a while for that to reach the R-devel builds[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4403223Z [36;1m# CI installs, so the wrapper is still doing real work here. It stays[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4403664Z [36;1m# after that too: it costs nothing and is correct either way.[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4403994Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4404314Z [36;1m# Windows deliberately keeps the plain prefix, as a control group: it is[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4404815Z [36;1m# where a repeat of that upstream change would show up, while the Unix[0m
2026-08-22T02:04:04.4405192Z [36;1m# jobs carry on regardless.[0m
